<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Goldman likes Bank/Scotland.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Goldman likes Bank/Scotland.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Scotland Plc was added to Goldman Sachs' model portfolio of European banking stocks, reflecting the brokerage's enthusiasm for the company's prospects, market sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Sources said Bank of Scotland was Goldman's second favourite UK banking stock behind HSBC Holdings Plc. It replaced Barclays Plc in Goldman's banking portfolio, but sources said this did not reflect any negative view on Barclays.</p>
<p>Analysts at the brokerage were not immediately available for comment. Bank of Scotland shares were down 2-1/2p at 276 and Barclays was down 2p at 954-1/2. HSBC was down 8p at 12.75 stg.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
